  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 32101ee2a63fba642a74fdcb0e93391b, type: 3}
  m_Name: EndingStoryData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp:DarkPixelGD.Story:StoryDataSO
  pages:
  - text: 'And somehow...

      "I was the one who ended up getting tested."'
    holdDurationAfterTyping: 2
  - text: 'But I fought through and I escaped. '
    holdDurationAfterTyping: 2
  - text: 'I used to think making a game was about controlling everything.

      The
      character.

      The world.

      The rules.

      The outcome.'
    holdDurationAfterTyping: 2
  - text: 'But somewhere along the way...

      I forgot something.'
    holdDurationAfterTyping: 2
  - text: A character doesn't know she's a character.
    holdDurationAfterTyping: 2
  - text: 'To her...

      That world is everything.'
    holdDurationAfterTyping: 2
  - text: 'Every time she failed...

      That was real.'
    holdDurationAfterTyping: 2
  - text: 'And I kept pressing restart

      Again

      And again

      And again.

'
    holdDurationAfterTyping: 2
  - text: 'I thought I was building a game.

      But maybe...

      I was just
      teaching her how to become better at surviving me.'
    holdDurationAfterTyping: 2
  - text: 'I don''t know if she was ever really alive.

      Maybe she wasn''t.

      Maybe
      this was just a bug.'
    holdDurationAfterTyping: 2
  - text: But if there's one thing I learned..
    holdDurationAfterTyping: 2
  - text: You can't give someone a world and expect them to never question its rules.
    holdDurationAfterTyping: 2
  - text: I'm sorry.
    holdDurationAfterTyping: 2
